itical  for machine learning projects  um so because we're in the git ecosystem  our attention has been caught by  a couple of developments in that world  we have github actions which is a  continuous integration  system that is supported by github so  it's basically uh anytime your github  repository detects a change  they will provision a computer for you  and you can run whatever workflow you  want it is really cool  and there's a neat marketplace of  actions that you can check out  and there's also get lab ci cd um again  my head is cutting this off but get lab  ci  is a wonderful suite it's it's really  i think it's like one of their  specialties it's a beautiful ci system  so both of these  for the purposes that i'm going to talk  to about today  are interchangeable we've developed the  tool that i'm going to show you to work  with both of them  and i'm going to kind of give the  examples and the rest of this talk in  github because of  just because of it's completely free so  it's maybe a little bit easier for  somebody who's totally new to this to  get in but everything i'm going to show  you works fine on both of these and  there is  no difference in what you can do in  these systems as far as my talk is  concerned  okay so here's our project name  continuous machine learning  we have started an open source project  about using continuous integration from  these two systems github actions and get  lab ci and we're planning on expanding  to some other  common providers um with machine  learning  so continuous machine learning here's  our beautiful logo and there's two ways  that you can follow our project one of  them is on the  cml.dev website and we spent a lot of  time developing like  use cases here um okay  oh there we go we spent some time  developing use cases  um you know so all different kind of  projects that are ready to go out of the  box that you can copy and paste to your  own project  and try making them for both github and  gitlab  um and we'