ing a docker container here so  i'm pulling first uh the operating  system for the runner  and that's for the machine that github  is provisioning for me  a runner managed by them i'm pulling the  docker container for the cml project  you can also use your own docker  container or you can use no docker  container  and so when this happens we're going to  run the following workflow we will  install some requirements  we're going to run a python train dot pi  is my script  and then we're going to uh use some cml  functions with and a little bit of batch  scripting here  um it's it's fairly mundane stuff and  then we're going to use this to write  a markdown file report.markdown  and we're going to use cml to deliver  that markdown  file and i'll show you what that means  essentially  when you make a pull request you get a  report  and it appears as a comment in the pull  request so  here you can see that we've got you know  we made a commit  on this pull request and we printed out  the accuracy of the model that was  trained by pythontrain.pi  and we printed out a picture and the  picture is an ordinary  png file it's not special in any way  and so the value of having this appear  in your pull request  is that now this result from your model  training  is visible to your team and when you  decide if you want to  merge this model into your you know the  main branch of your project  you have this available to you and it's  always linked to the commit  that generated it so  hopefully when you have this you and  your team can have a more informed  discussion  and a conversation about whether or not  this is merge worthy  let's take a closer look at what exactly  is run in the workflow  we have a training script that outputs a  text file of  metrics and a confusion matrix so the  first thing we do is we do some bash  scripting  to take the contents of metrics.text put  them in the markdown report  then we're going to use this publish  function that we we've created here  t